second artist, birth date for a different person, or second sport is evidence to retain it. Check each proposed deletion once more against all originals before producing the final short list.\nInput: {\"question\": \"Who won the 5th Soccer Bowl?\", \"slot_hint\": \"person\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0019-60e220b9848a:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 143, \"text\": \"NASL Final 1973 NASL Final 1973 was the championship match of the 1973 season, between the expansion Philadelphia Atoms and the Dallas Tornado.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0019-60e220b9848a:d00\", \"start\": 144, \"end\": 218, \"text\": \"The match was played on August 25, 1973 at Texas Stadium in Irving, Texas.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0019-60e220b9848a:d00\", \"start\": 219, \"end\": 327, \"text\": \"The Philadelphia Atoms won the match, 2–0, and were crowned the 1973 North American Soccer League champions.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0019-60e220b9848a:d00\", \"start\": 328, \"end\": 433, \"text\": \"The Dallas Tornado qualified for the playoffs by virtue of winning the Southern Division with 111 points.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0019-60e220b9848a:d00\", \"start\": 434, \"end\": 550, \"text\": \"They also had the highest point-total in the NASL, and therefore were guaranteed home field throughout the playoffs.\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0019-60e220b9848a:d00\", \"start\": 551, \"end\": 616, \"text\": \"They defeated the defending champion New York Cosmos, 1–0, in the\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0019-60e220b9848a:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 42, \"text\": \"game , losing to Vancouver Whitecaps 1–2 .\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0019-60e220b9848a:d01\", \"start\": 43, \"end\": 110, \"text\": \"The next year , the Fury would go on to become the Montreal Manic .\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0019-60e220b9848a:d01\", \"start\": 111, \"end\": 215, \"text\": \"Philadelphia soccer fans would have to wait 30 years for the return of professional soccer to the city .\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0019-60e220b9848a:d01\", \"start\": 216, \"end\": 352, \"text\": \"Philadelphia Atoms v Dallas Tornado , 1973 NASL Championship Final Check out our two-part history of the Philadelphia Atoms : Part One .\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0019-60e220b9848a:d01\", \"start\": 353, \"end\": 363, \"text\": \"Part Two .\"}, \"D2S6\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0019-60e220b9848a:d01\", \"start\": 364, \"end\": 459, \"text\": \"Share this : Twitter Facebook More Reddit Email Author : Ed Farnsworth Editor-at-large at PSP .\"}, \"D2S7\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0019-60e220b9848a:d01\", \"start\": 460, \"end\": 552, \"text\": \"His work has also appeared at Philly.com , TheCup.us , Society for American Soccer History ,\"}, \"D3S1\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0019-60e220b9848a:d02\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 446, \"text\": \"Toros Minnesota Kicks Minnesota Strikers Montreal Manic Montreal Olympique New England Tea Men New York Cosmos New York Generals New York Skyliners 1 Oakland Clippers Oakland Stompers Philadelphia Spartans 2 Philadelphia Atoms Philadelphia Fury Pittsburgh Phantoms 2 Portland Timbers Rochester Lancers San Antonio Thunder San Diego Jaws San Diego Sockers San Diego Toros San Francisco Golden Gate Gales 1 San Jose Earthquakes Seattle Sounders St.\"}, \"D3S2\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0019-60e220b9848a:d02\", \"start\": 447, \"end\": 713, \"text\": \"Louis Stars Tampa Bay Rowdies Team America Team Hawaii Toronto Blizzard Toronto City 1 Toronto Metros Toronto Metros-Croatia Tulsa Roughnecks Vancouver Royals Vancouver Whitecaps Washington Darts Washington Diplomats Washington Whips 1 United Soccer Association team\"}, \"D4S1\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0019-60e220b9848a:d03\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 467, \"text\": \"Cubillas Fort Lauderdale Strikers 30 16 18 50 Alan Willey Minnesota Kicks 29 21 7 49 Dennis Tueart New York Cosmos 27 16 16 48 Laurie Abrahams California/Tulsa 25 18 9 45 Johan Cruyff Los Angeles Aztecs 23 13 16 42 Goalkeeping [ edit ] Note : GP = Games played ; Min - Minutes played ; GA = Goals against ; GAA = Goals against average ; W = Wins ; L = Losses ; SO = Shutouts Player Team GP Min SV GA GAA W L SO Phil Parkes Vancouver Whitecaps 29 2704 100 29 0.96 20 9\"}, \"D5S1\": {\"document_number\": 5, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0019-60e220b9848a:d04\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 74, \"text\": \"2024 2025 Note : there is no clear information from CSA about tier of U.S.\"}, \"D5S2\": {\"document_number\": 5, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0019-60e220b9848a:d04\", \"start\": 75, \"end\": 116, \"text\": \"based leagues which have Canadian clubs .\"}, \"D5S3\": {\"document_number\": 5, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0019-60e220b9848a:d04\", \"start\": 117, \"end\": 214, \"text\": \"In terms of historical information , they have been deployed as tier 1 league as USSF have done .\"}, \"D5S4\": {\"document_number\": 5, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0019-60e220b9848a:d04\", \"start\": 215, \"end\": 273, \"text\": \"Retrieved from `` https : //en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php ?\"}, \"D5S5\": {\"document_number\": 5, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0019-60e220b9848a:d04\", \"start\": 274, \"end\": 660, \"text\": \"title=1979_North_American_Soccer_League_season & oldid=1229900451 `` Categories : 1979 North American Soccer League season North American Soccer League ( 1968–1984 ) seasons 1979 in American soccer 1979 in Canadian soccer Hidden categories : Articles with short description Short description is different from Wikidata Use mdy dates from February 2023 Use American English from February\"}}, \"origina